      "value": "@{64873f159cf028090ce2c2e2|full_name} - I don't know how to record yet. (I'm willing to learn)\n\nBut I think I found a problem. Some of the avatars I use are labeled 'Very Poor' in quality. In Quest's settings, I cannot disable the avatar autoblock that only has 'Very Poor' and 'Poor & Below' as its options. And since nearly every avatar we use is in the Very Poor range, I cannot see what they want to use.\n\nMy friend noted that Quest users SHOULD see the Quest-version of avatars that have them. But I've never seen any that work.\n\nQuestion: Is the autoblock feature preventing me from seeing a PC user's avatar, even if it's the same one I'm using?",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
